{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-05-17T02:28:08.426Z","evidence":{"commit":"7645a96e7ef55fdb45ac2056c3d21328b5180889"},"name":"recover-zombie-wip-feature-only","description":"When recovering crashed builder WIP whose cumulative diff also deletes hook source files, use 'git checkout <wip-branch> -- <feature-paths-only>' from a fresh dev branch instead of merging or cherry-picking. Path-scoped checkout omits the hook deletions atomically. Verify with 'git diff --name-only dev <wip-branch>' first to enumerate paths, exclude any out-of-scope deletions, then run pnpm install (NODE_ENV=development for devDeps), pnpm db:generate, pnpm stack:up (bridge auto-applies migration), pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm test:integration && pnpm probe:smoke. Resource singletons (PUT-only, no POST) trigger RESOURCE_GRAPH_NO_CREATE_ENDPOINT diagnostic — expected, not failure.","id":"mx-d64097"}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-05-17T08:51:33.005Z","evidence":{"commit":"c02f16dfb4a862da45598b519b6ec816e820bf26"},"name":"ship-merger-cherry-pick-skip-wip-zombie","description":"Ship-merger pattern: when builder branch tip is post-code-complete WIP-ZOMBIE-RECOVERY auto-commits, do NOT git-merge the branch tip. Coordinator pins code-complete SHA in dispatch. Cherry-pick only non-WIP commits in order. git merge of intermediate SHA is blocked by pre-merge worktree-mapping check; cherry-pick bypasses cleanly. Verify with full gate chain afterward.","id":"mx-f7b7e3"}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-05-17T09:23:25.389Z","evidence":{"commit":"cb7bda7cc3c1fe67dfbb46707520561fbad52286"},"name":"ship-merger-NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL-shell-override-workaround","description":"Ship-merger workaround when scripts/stack-up-docker.sh omits NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL from its env-export block (lines 345-347): docker-compose interpolates empty, Dockerfile build ARG empty, /app/apps/web/.env.local overwritten empty, execute-request.ts falls back to http://localhost:3001 (ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED in browser). Workaround: invoke 'NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://app.localtest.me:APP_PROXY_PORT pnpm stack:reset && (same env) pnpm stack:up' to inject the value via shell, which compose then propagates through the build ARG AND runtime env paths. No source-code change required in worktree. Mail coordinator to land the permanent fix (add NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to the export list in stack-up-docker.sh). write_web_env_local helper also writes API_PORT not APP_PROXY_PORT — secondary bug shadowed by the build-time overwrite, but worth noting in same escalation.","files":["scripts/stack-up-docker.sh"],"id":"mx-dfe443"}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-05-17T18:57:23.381Z","evidence":{"commit":"04341fe9454ee360ce30a3cfdfeea51e157f9cb9"},"outcomes":[{"status":"success","agent":"builder-bg-chunk-a-v4"}],"dir_anchors":[".claude/hooks",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring",".claude/skills/task-flow-authoring"],"name":"vitest-integration-dotenv-loader","description":"vitest-integration.config.ts has no setupFiles to load apps/api/.env, so fresh shell pnpm test:integration fails Prisma init with Environment variable not found DATABASE_URL. Per-module __integration__/setup-env.ts must load .env itself via fs.readFileSync plus parse OR caller must inline DATABASE_URL on shell. company-info setup-env does not load so fails on clean shell. brand setup-env loads via tiny inline parser so passes. Long-term fix add load to test/vitest-integration.config.ts.","files":[".claude/hooks/no-close-without-source-probes.js",".claude/hooks/no-merge-without-source-probes.js",".claude/hooks/validate-flow-file.js",".claude/settings.json",".claude/skills/feature-plan/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/flow-failure-response/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/product-plan/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/_shared-management.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/bootstrap-and-curate.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/cross-task-flows.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/failure-modes.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-async.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-bulk.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-business-rule.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-concurrency.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-content-negotiation.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-cross-call-invariant.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-cross-resource-chain.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-cross-tenant.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-endpoint.md","