{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-05-17T21:34:42.440Z","evidence":{"commit":"b10fbc412c1de7b28b36eb5a584a12026c79e667"},"outcomes":[{"status":"success","agent":"builder-bg-chunk-c-v1"}],"dir_anchors":[".claude/hooks",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring",".claude/skills/task-flow-authoring"],"name":"brand-guidelines-sibling-module-with-cross-token","description":"When a NestJS module needs read-only access to a sibling module's repository token (e.g. BRAND_REPOSITORY in brand.module.ts which doesn't export it) AND the sibling's module file is out of scope, register a local provider via useFactory: () => new SiblingRepository(prisma). The @Inject decorator on the repo's constructor is metadata for the DI container — direct construction via new bypasses it. This avoids editing the sibling module to add to exports[] and avoids circular module imports. Pattern used in apps/api/src/modules/brand-guidelines/brand-guidelines.module.ts to inject BrandRepository read-only from the brand module without modifying brand.module.ts (mx-3bf156 carve-out).","files":[".claude/hooks/no-close-without-source-probes.js",".claude/hooks/no-merge-without-source-probes.js",".claude/hooks/validate-flow-file.js",".claude/settings.json",".claude/skills/feature-plan/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/flow-failure-response/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/product-plan/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/SKILL.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/_shared-management.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/bootstrap-and-curate.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/cross-task-flows.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/failure-modes.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-async.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-bulk.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-business-rule.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-concurrency.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/per-content-negotiation.md",".claude/skills/shared-flow-authoring/